 "result_text": "I fixed the intermittent `test_add_dataset` failure; I didn't look into `test_encoders.py::TestDatasetCompress::test_round_trip`. `tests/test_uid.py` and `tests/test_fileset.py` pass (193 tests).\n\nThe cause was in `generate_uid()` in `src/pydicom/uid.py`. When a prefix is given, it appended a random number below `10 ** (64 - len(prefix))`. That number sometimes had fewer digits than the maximum, so the UID could be shorter than 64 characters. A shorter UID changed the encoded length of the directory dataset, which gave the 398 vs 396 mismatch.\n\n`generate_uid()` now always produces a suffix with the full number of digits and no leading zero. UIDs made with a prefix are therefore always 64 characters long. If the prefix is already 64 characters, it returns the prefix unchanged.\n\nI only ran those two test files, not the full suite, and I didn't repeat runs to confirm the flakiness is gone. I didn't touch the `test_round_trip` failure, which the issue guesses is a memory re-use problem.",
